# /etc/cron.d/openmarquee-daily-restart
#
# Belt-and-braces companion to openmarquee-cma-watchdog.timer.
# The watchdog catches CMA pressure that crosses 254MB (r59 default;
# was 220 in r38c, raised for v1.0.1); this cron
# catches slow drift that stays below the watchdog threshold but
# would still wedge over multi-day uptime.
#
# Fires at 03:00 local time -- Pi system TZ is intentionally local
# per the schedule.py contract. Restart costs ~3-8s of black screen
# during the slowest viewer hour.
#
# Bridges until r38b's actual leak fix lands. See
# qa/r38c-cma-pressure-watchdog-2026-06-02.md.
#
# Format: m h dom mon dow user command
0 3 * * * root /bin/systemctl restart --no-block openmarquee-backend.service
